Implemented `phone_number.py` with the canonical NANP cleaner:
- `_clean` strips all non-digit characters, drops a leading `1` from 11-digit numbers, rejects anything not exactly 10 digits, and rejects area/exchange codes starting with `0` or `1` (raises `ValueError`).
- Exposes `.number`, `.area_code`, and `.pretty()` → `(NXX) NXX-XXXX`.

